# USBCloudBackup — Remediation Implementation Plan

> **Specification State**: FINAL APPROVED SPECIFICATION — READY FOR IMPLEMENTATION REVIEW  
> **Target Systems**: `USBCloudBackup` (Android Ingestion Agent & Cloudflare Worker B2 Authorizer)  
> **Application ID**: `com.usbcloudbackup`  
> **Cloud Storage**: Backblaze B2 (`BrightCloud` bucket via S3-compatible API & Scoped SigV4 Presigned URLs)  
> **Zero Code Edits Applied Yet**: Awaiting explicit user approval before modifying code.

---

## 1. Goal Description

This implementation plan resolves the audited bugs in the `USBCloudBackup` repository across three priority tiers (**P0**, **P1**, and **P2**), while strictly preserving all existing system invariants:
- **Universal Automatic File Upload**: Every readable regular user file discovered on an attached USB device (`.mp4`, `.mp3`, `.zip`, `.apk`, `.iso`, unknown extensions, extensionless files) is automatically hashed, deduplicated, and streamed to Backblaze B2. (BUG-08 remains explicitly rejected).
- **Headless Android Daemon**: The Android app acts strictly as an upload engine with no permanent user-facing monitoring dashboard. (BUG-10 remains explicitly rejected).
- **Zero Root B2 Credentials in Android APK**: All cloud storage operations use short-lived SigV4 presigned URLs generated by the Cloudflare Worker authorizer.
- **Document-Specific Download Authorization**: Friend download authorization uses a direct Firestore document read for `vaults/{vaultId}/files/{fileId}`, deriving the B2 object key from the authorized document rather than accepting arbitrary client-supplied paths. `/settings/config` remains strictly Google-Admin only.
- **Legacy Record Safety**: Backward-compatible fallback logic ensures legacy `contentHashes` records lacking denormalized metadata do not fail or crash the ingestion pipeline.
- **Duplicate Qualification Safety**: A file may only cause another identical file to be `SKIPPED_DUPLICATE` if canonical bytes already exist in B2 (`INDEXED` or `UPLOADED_NOT_INDEXED`). `NAME_RESERVED` and `UPLOADING` are strictly excluded from qualifying duplicate statuses.
- **Robust Dynamic USB Detach Delivery**: Dynamically registered receiver for `ACTION_USB_DEVICE_DETACHED` uses `ContextCompat.RECEIVER_EXPORTED` to guarantee delivery of system broadcasts across Android API 24–36 without leaking receivers or racing cancellations.

