#### [MODIFY] `app/src/main/java/com/usbcloudbackup/backup/DeduplicationEngine.kt`
- **Fix BUG-07**: Restrict qualifying local duplicate statuses strictly to statuses where cloud bytes are guaranteed to exist in B2:
```kotlin
// Strictly enforce: canonical bytes already exist in B2 (INDEXED or UPLOADED_NOT_INDEXED).
// NAME_RESERVED and UPLOADING are excluded as neither guarantees cloud bytes nor offline recovery.
val qualifyingStatuses = setOf(
    FileStatus.INDEXED,
    FileStatus.UPLOADED_NOT_INDEXED
)

val existingFile = fileRepository.findExistingFileByHash(hash)

if (existingFile != null && existingFile.id != file.id && existingFile.status in qualifyingStatuses) {
    fileRepository.updateFileStatus(file.id, FileStatus.SKIPPED_DUPLICATE)
    jobRepository.incrementSkipped(file.jobId)
    return DeduplicationResult.SkippedDuplicate(existingFile.id, hash)
}
```

#### [MODIFY] `app/src/main/java/com/usbcloudbackup/database/dao/FileDao.kt` & `FileRepository.kt`
- Update `findFileBySha256` or add `findValidDuplicateBySha256` to ensure queries specifically look for files in qualifying statuses:
```kotlin
@Query("SELECT * FROM files WHERE sha256 = :sha256 AND status IN ('INDEXED', 'UPLOADED_NOT_INDEXED') ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1")
suspend fun findValidDuplicateBySha256(sha256: String): FileEntity?
```
This prevents an un-uploaded or failed file record from masking an existing `INDEXED` file.

#### [MODIFY] `app/src/main/java/com/usbcloudbackup/worker/BackupWorker.kt` (Step 7 Just-In-Time Check)
- In Step 7 (Uploading loop): Before initiating an upload for each candidate in `uploadableFiles`, perform a just-in-time check:
```kotlin
// Check if an earlier identical file in the same batch or concurrent run just finished uploading
val localDedup = deduplicationEngine.checkLocalDeduplication(file)
if (localDedup is DeduplicationResult.SkippedDuplicate) {
    Log.i(TAG, "File ${file.originalName} resolved to duplicate of ${localDedup.existingFileId} before upload. Skipping bytes.")
    continue
}
```
If File A crashed before upload, File B does NOT skip and proceeds to upload its bytes. Exactly one file uploads bytes to B2, guaranteeing zero data loss.

